  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 246 AM CDT Wed Aug 19 2026\n\nUpper ridging then begins to establish across the Rockies and \namplifies into the weekend. This brings increasing warm advection, \nwith highs return to the upper 80s to lower 90s for late week and \nthis weekend. The warmest day look to be Friday, where portions of \nwestern and southwest Nebraska may approach the lower to middle 90s. \nThe threat for storms also looks to persist into Friday and beyond, \nwith ample flow aloft keeping strong deep layer shear in place. \nFriday looks of particular concern across portions of the Sandhills, \nwhere backed southeasterly surface winds suggests some threat for \nincreased low-level shear as well. With deep moisture remaining in \nplace, a favorable overlap of instability and shear exists for \nsevere storms across the area Friday afternoon and evening. Some \nthreat for severe storms may persist into the weekend as well. \nGuidance then diverges somewhat into next week, though still point \ntowards continued northwest flow aloft. This suggests that the \nthreat for near daily storms may persist across the area into next \nweek.",
